  <!-- ===== How I Work ===== -->
  <section id="work">
    <h2>How I Work</h2>
    <p class="standfirst">How I handle access to your systems, and what I will and won't do with your records.</p>

    <div class="principle">
      <b>The least access that does the job.</b>
      <p>For anything involving data, whether billing, subscriptions, contracts, or CRM records, I work from exports and never need a login. For workspace builds and restructures I need edit rights on the specific pages in scope, never admin and never the whole workspace. If external access isn't possible at all, I build in a separate workspace and hand the finished thing over, or deliver the structure and rewritten pages for your team to implement.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="principle">
      <b>No credentials, ever.</b>
      <p>I don't take passwords or shared logins for anything. Where access is needed it's granted through the tool's own permissions and can be revoked in one click.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="principle">
      <b>Nothing gets deleted.</b>
      <p>Superseded records and pages are archived with a note on why. Merges and structural changes are proposed for approval, not executed silently.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="principle">
      <b>Findings, not opinions.</b>
      <p>Every figure traces back to a calculation or a named clause. Where the answer genuinely isn't knowable, it's written down as an open question rather than filled in with a guess.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

